rent gifts  based on the solution by delivering  blood and souls to this version of The  Box the user can reach new levels of  experience and even choose their fate  when reaching the cenobites god  Leviathan this adds a certain depth to  the story of the box which is  particularly clear when Riley discovers  that Voigt survived his encounter with  the artifact though he was transformed  into a being in constant pain by the  cenobites this suggests that more than  one person has in some form lived to  tell the tale of the box and their  adventures with it and if the right  person picks up that trail they just  might find a trove of new information  Riley leaves the Box behind suggesting  she's not the person to keep  investigating its Secrets but that  doesn't mean the blocks will be  abandoned forever if we've learned  anything from this franchise so far  someone else is bound to grow curious  activate the box and search for new  truths about its history what they find  and how it changes them seems like  perfect fodder for a sequel  because Voigt survived his encounter  with Leviathan at the end of his first  journey with the puzzle box he can  impart certain information about what  the cenobites are and what they want as  he explains to Riley every choice the  beings present to the user of the box is  a trick a doorway to some Untold pain  that varies based on the user but  nevertheless always comes back to  suffering  I saw the pleasure  with all they have to give  his pain  in his quest to give back his gift the  liminal configuration which pushes his  nerve endings to maximum pain at every  opportunity Voigt puts more and more  people In Harm's Way only to be told at  the End by the hell priest that there is  no retreat once the threshold has been  crossed all he can do is make an  exchange at the hell priest's behest he  chooses the Leviathan configuration  granting him the power that his true  nature was always seeking what he  doesn't know and what the last scene  reveals is that this means he will  become a cenobite in service to the  constant pursuit of Anguish the film  leaves us without a clear picture of  voit's cenobite future but it seems  quite possible that a sequel would see  him standing side by side with the hell  priest working the dark magic of the  cenobites on others what this means for  his human form his memories and other  aspects of the man he was remains to be  seen  as with the original Hellraiser we're  introduced to the lead cenobite  popularly known as Pinhead  in the new movie they're known in this  film as the hell priest the monster  exists to fulfill their role as a  servant of the puzzle box we never learn  much about the hell priest's backstory  most of what we know about the character  is from their role in the story not how  Hell priest came to be or why but that  doesn't mean the hell priest is without  personality at least twice in the film  we see the creature react with surprise  amusement or both as their order is  challenged by both Voigt and Riley in  different ways this suggests that the  hell priest like their predecessor is  not immune to Bargains compromises or  simply intriguing new configurations of  the order they've established with any  luck future films could grant us some  more personal detailed look at who and  what the hell priest is much as  Hellbound Hellraiser 2 does and what led  them to choose the Leviathan  configuration and ultimately become a  cenobite in the process we might learn  what continues to drive this character  and what if anything they hope to gain  from continuing to fulfill the role for  all eternity  as Hellraiser goes on we get more and  more insights into Voigt and his  years-long search for the furthest  reaches of human experience which  included turning his Mansion into not  just a museum but an elaborate puzzle  box of sorts in and of itself it's a  home filled with secret rooms artifacts  and automated features including a  complex metal cage that wraps around the  entire structure with the flick of a few  switches eventually it's revealed that  the cage was designed by Voigt  specifically to trap the cenobites in  place allowing him to demand they remove  his liminal gift and free him from his  life of constant pain of course the  outside world doesn't know this or at  least they don't know it yet Riley may  tell her story to an interested party  perhaps the authorities will get wind of  the place and investigate regardless  it's likely that someone is going to  make their way out to Voight's Mansion  again and they're going to find a  chamber of Horrors that includes the  puzzle box still on the floor where  Riley left it what that means for the  future of the Box isn't clear but it's  likely someone somewhere knows exactly  what it is and what to do with it if  we've learned any anything from  Hellraiser films it's that these sort of  hidden places never stay hidden long  because the human pursuit of desires  never ceases almost everyone connected  to The Saga of the puzzle box and David  bruckner's Hellraiser dies one way or  another but Riley is not the only  Survivor of this particular story Cullen  the devoted partner to Riley's dead  brother and devoted friend to Riley  herself also manages to survive this is  thanks to Riley's last second decision  to leave Trevor to these cenobites  rather than let Colin die Colin's not a  major decision maker in the story at  least not in terms of the major moves  regarding the box and the cenobites but  he does have a crucial role to play now  like Riley he has to get on with his  life but what does that life look like  now that Colin has seen these Horrors  he's clearly not intrigued by them in  the same way other characters are but  they will remain imprinted on his brain  nevertheless it seems likely based on  the end of the film that he'll stay at  least somewhat close to Riley but as she  attempts to live a regular life with her  difficult history what does that mean  for Colin will he be able to find love  again does he have the horrible  distinction like White's former  associate of being cursed by the contact  he had with the box it's not clear but  the the road forward for a guy who's  been through this much won't be easy  though it delves into the secret of the  puzzle box more than any other single  previous Hellraiser installment the new  Hellraiser film still leaves numerous  questions about the box and its magical  properties unanswered we know what it  does and how it works but there are so  many other wrinkles that future films  could explore so many dark angles within  its various configurations the film  shows us that there are loopholes within  the rules of the box for instance there  is the Revelation that cenobites can be  sacrificed as victims as users of the  Box move through the various  configurations does that mean there are  other ways to summon and manipulate  cenobites Voigt found a way to restrain  them in his research which suggests  there are other stimuli and phenomena  they respond to and there's the more  straightforward question of how someone  gets such an artifact in the first place  are there dealers out there who  specifically traffic in such things  that's a question that seems ripe for a  sequel all its own  as with Hellbound Hellraiser 2 the new  Hellraiser film establishes the  existence of Leviathan a god figure the  cenobites serve but there are a few  tweaks to the mythology this time  Leviathan in this film retains the look  and feel that it had in Hellbound but  has the added power to grant wishes  these wishes exist because now the user  of the box is not automatically dragged  off to Hell by the cenobites instead  they're given one of a handful of  choices to make as the Box changes  configurations though the film doesn't  spend all that much time exploring the  depths and meaning of leviathan the very  existence of this being is both  fascinating and ripe for deeper  exploration and potential sequels what  else does Leviathan do is it just as  powerful as the biblical God are there  other ways to summon it how many  cenobites does it command and where do  they reside the ending of the film which  transforms Voit into a new cenobite  suggests a sequel might give us a more  thorough look at this story's version of  hell and that would be a welcome journey  in this newly reinvigorated franchise  unlike the puzzle box in previous films  the box in the new Hellraiser offers  more than one Pathway to new experiences  as Riley learns by going through  Voight's research the Box goes through  six different configurations and when  its wielders reach the end of the puzzle  they're able to choose one of six  different paths when you choose your  ultimate desire  life knowledge love sensation power  Resurrection  we see how three of these play out in  the film as Riley chooses lament and  Voit chooses first liminal and then  Leviathan but as Voit warns Riley before  he makes a second choice the consequence  of every decision is a trick by the  cenobites all they have to offer he  cautions is pain this of course begs the  question what do the other three  configurations do Riley considers  choosing Lazarus to bring her brother  back from the dead but stops when she  realizes it's likely a trap what about  the other two how far do they go in  transforming a human body into something  horrific where their gift of knowledge  transform you into a living brain  without a moment's piece does the gift  of love shroud you in such devotion that  you can never escape the one who loves  you nor they you these are excellent  little tidbits of the Mythos and would  make wonderful sequel fodder at the end  of the film when Riley could choose the  Lazarus configuration to potentially  bring her brother back she instead  chooses to live I know my brother's gone  this is the lament configuration it  represents a willingness to endure the  bitter and brief realm of human life  unaugmented it's a life that the  cinebites believe is full of regret and  mundane suffering it seems like the  right choice at the moment and it even  makes the cenobites return to their  realm but in the car with Colin at the  end of the film Riley doesn't look so  sure Colin asks her if her choice was  the right one and she doesn't have an  immediate answer it suggests that her  addictive personality wonders what might  happen if she goes back and picks up the  box again it would be so easy to take it  with her just in case just to see if she  might like to try a different  configuration one day it might even be  worth it to get her brother back even if  he's different than he was before  whether she changes her mind or not it's  clear Riley will be haunted by her  choice for a very long time and that  haunting might be worth exploring in  future films  [Music]

